diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..046549f 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -101,6 +101,26 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send push notifications to people's phones and desktops, so that anything that lands in their notification tray also reaches them outside the app.
+To enable this you need to provide a VAPID key pair, which Fizzy uses to identify itself to the browser push services.
+
+Generate a key pair with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then pass both values to the container:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=... --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=... ...
+```
+
+You can also set `VAPID_SUBJECT` to a `mailto:` or `https:` contact address for your instance (it defaults to `mailto:support@fizzy.do`).
+If these variables are not set, push notifications stay turned off and the setting is hidden.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
